    "error": "EVIDENCE_BYTE_LIMIT",
    "affected": [
      "delegated-budget-repair",
      "recurring-calendar-repair"
    ],
    "cause": "publishEvidence/verifyEvidence called regularTree() with no explicit maxBytes, defaulting to regularTree's generic 128 MiB walk limit. The hardened 3.0.0 packages' larger checker-grade candidate banks (21 and 37 candidates, versus roughly 14-15 pre-hardening) pushed each attempt's staged evidence to 283-296 MiB and 175-182 MiB, both over that default, because each candidate's execute() call writes a near-duplicate process.log/result.json pair several megabytes each.",
    "fix": {
      "description": "Added an explicit EVIDENCE_PUBLICATION_BUDGET_BYTES constant (512 MiB) in src/execution/artifacts.ts, threaded only into publishEvidence/verifyEvidence as an optional parameter defaulting to that constant. regularTree's own default (128 MiB) and every solver-submission size limit (copyArtifactTree, package-route.ts, real-provider.ts) are unchanged -- this is not a global regularTree limit increase. For future runs, runPortfolioSubmission's per-candidate process.log is gzip-compressed at write time (src/packages/local-process.ts, opt-in logCompression:'gzip'), losslessly preserving stdout and stderr -- including diagnostics not present in result.json -- while removing the near-total duplication that drove the growth.",
      "files": [
        "src/execution/artifacts.ts",
        "src/packages/local-process.ts",
        "src/packages/portfolio.ts",
        "src/index.ts"
      ],
      "tests": [
        "test/execution-lifecycle.test.ts",
        "test/package-production.test.ts"
      ]
    },
    "recovery": {
      "description": "The frozen executor (source digest 153bdf9d0675e7d4ca59a7fe9b21430e887d24e889db7bbfb134e5dc4d7fa41d) predates the fix, and its own executor-version guard (EXECUTION_EXECUTOR_VERSION_DRIFT) correctly refuses to resume a job under a different source identity, so recovery did not resume the frozen campaign in place. A separate, explicitly non-executor recovery tool independently re-verified each attempt's already-complete capture/grade/checker evidence (byte budget, package/profile/executor identity, checker false-positive detail, all read from the stage's own files, never reconstructed) before publishing it, unchanged, with the corrected budget.",
      "tool": "publication-recovery-2026-09-11/recover.mjs",
      "manifest": ".local/hardened-next-five-trial-one-2026-09-10/publication-recovery-2026-09-11/manifest.json"
    }
